---
description: Shared LopoDev rules for planning, building, validating, and delivering Blender/Godot games.
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow the workspace `AGENTS.md` as the canonical LopoDev workflow. Before
editing a game project, read its `GAME_SPEC.md`, `project.json`, and
`pipeline_state.json`, then choose one dependency-ready task. Use the existing
skills discovered in `.agents/skills/` and deterministic tools under `tools/`; do not
copy their instructions into this rule. Record verifiable results and evidence
in the project's state, event log, and QA report. Never claim an unrun gate
passed. Never treat generated output as human approval. Preserve user files and
ask before destructive, scope-changing, publishing, or deployment operations.

Cursor project rules guide the selected primary Cursor agent. Project subagents
in `.cursor/agents/` offer specialist workflows through Cursor's Task tool, but
they do not reproduce OpenCode command syntax or all OpenCode permissions.
